# Default --session-log output, written to the current directory on
# every run unless --session-log/--no-session-log says otherwise.
# README's own 実行方法 section says to run from the project root, so
# this is exactly where every default-configured run leaves it --
# confirmed directly by running the real session-logging path from
# this directory and watching `git status` immediately offer to track
# it. Ignored so a session actually run here (for a quick manual
# check, say) doesn't show up as something to `git add`.
